WEBVTT

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.750
Target captured!

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.940
<i>Timothy, sitrep?</i>

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.160
I captured three members of 
both the star and moon teams.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.040
So only the four-leaf clover team 
still has all of its members.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.880
Hanakoizumi-san and her 
friends are working hard.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.130
Ren, where are you?!

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.190
Actually, where am I?

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.850
Oh, my.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.290
I, uh... I-I'm glad I ran into you!

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.370
There's something I want to say!

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.440
Is that so? Go ahead, then.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.860
All right, I will.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.760
You call this "tag"?!

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.410
What's the point in playing
a crazy game like this?

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.080
This is a test, too.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.350
In this forest, avoiding capture 
until the end of the game

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.490
<b>Futon</b>

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.490
and finding your wooden carvings

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.550
will take luck in addition to 
intelligence and fortitude.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:18.010
But Hagyu-san, you seem to have 
fallen victim to your own bad luck.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.760
A-Anyway, that's all I had to say!

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.600
Farewell!

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.060
You think you can escape?

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.180
You saved me.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:09.750
This is Kumegawa-san's...

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:13.300
I need to meet up with the others, right?

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.860
But first...

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.900
I'm tired, so I'll take a nap.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.130
So fluffy...

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.760
What's going on?

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.320
She seems even more intense than usual!

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.090
But...

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.080
I'll simply defeat the enemy before me.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.350
That's how I, Hibiki, live my life 
settling for no less than first place!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.030
Just watch how the former ace of 
the track and field team runs!

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.560
Ace of long-distance races, that is...

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.270
Oh, no—

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.830
It's dangerous to shout while running.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.120
T-Teacher...

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.370
Well, now that you're out, 
you don't need to run anymore.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.860
Damn it!

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.740
Ti-Ti-Timo Timo, Mi-Timo Timothy!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:28.520
Ti-Ti-Timo Timo, tell me how you feel!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.520
You'll attract the real Timothys.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.660
Stop that.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:35.240
The entire forest seems
to be surrounded by a wall.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.650
Is this why they call it Miniature Garden Tag?

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.020
The weather sure is nice.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.150
It's starting to get hot, though.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.970
I didn't put on any sunscreen.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.160
Why not cover up with a towel?

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.120
I'll put it on for you!

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.730
Maybe not...

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.630
Aww, but you looked so cute!

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.290
I was going to do the same thing 
so we could start a bandit group.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.930
Take it, thieves!

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.010
You know, like Robin Hood's Merry Men.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.590
Why now?

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.210
Because...

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.720
Hanako, watch out behind you.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.310
Huh?

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.110
It's a Toxicodendron succedaneum.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.270
It'll give you a rash if you 
touch it, so be careful.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.660
It's not as bad as the T. trichocarpum 
or T. orientale, though.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.830
Toxico...

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.480
I did notice...

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:25.490
that this forest has an unnaturally 
low number of poisonous plants.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.720
Maybe this is another facility

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.700
created for the happiness class, 
like the school's basement.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.660
That's amazing!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.440
But was a game of tag worth all this?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.540
No, I meant that you're amazing, Hibari-chan.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.130
Me?

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.680
You knew what it was at a glance.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.010
You're a plant doctor!

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.640
I'm nothing like that.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.220
It's not like I studied it because I wanted to.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.020
And when it comes to plants, they know more.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.000
They?

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.230
N-Never mind!

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.760
Let's go. I refuse to sleep outside
because we placed last.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.980
All right!

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.990
<b>Hibari's
Bandits</b>

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.300
Take it, thieves!

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:05.960
Tug.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:09.900
Now I don't need a parasol.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.390
I've caused nothing but trouble for the others.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.010
It pains me so much that I can barely breathe.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.330
At the very least, I have to help
them find their carvings...

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.980
My eyes! My eyes!

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.700
My head...

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.060
This new body seems strong.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.050
I'm thirsty.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.620
I'm pretty sure I had water...

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.240
Where's my backpack?

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:46.780
Oh, right...

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.950
Wild grapes? Are those for me?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.080
And these? And these?

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.470
Don't do anything crazy.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.010
Thanks, everyone.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.450
But I can't eat all of this myself.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.410
Let's eat it together.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:19.860
Timo!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.780
There's nowhere to run.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:27.990
Too bad.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:32.860
I'm stuck...

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:37.850
How did you get stuck in a 
bottomless swamp out here?

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:40.210
You saved me. Thanks.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.570
Did you find that?

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:43.170
Yeah.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:47.420
There's a strap on it, so someone 
in our class must have carved it.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.210
You're probably right.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:51.080
It's not one of ours, though.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.900
It'll be safer to leave it here 
instead of near the swamp.

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:58.750
Brilliant idea, Hibari Hood!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.040
Who are you calling Hibari Hood?

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.510
<i>Hello, girls. Are you all doing your best?</i>

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.940
<i>It's almost eleven o'clock.</i>

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.190
What is this?!

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.570
How dare you keep me and Ren in 
a cage like a couple of prisoners?!

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.780
You won't get away with this!

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:16.830
You don't scare me at all.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.530
Isn't it more fun this way?

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:21.210
It's just a bit of fan service.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.140
Fan service, my butt!

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.000
In any case, isn't there
usually some kind of rule

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.700
that lets captured players 
get back in the game somehow?

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.130
Of course not.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.340
There isn't?

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:36.120
But that does sound interesting.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.060
If you're somehow able to escape, 
I'll allow you to keep playing.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.020
What?

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.730
There's no chance of that happening, though.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.600
Damn it!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.080
<i>Ms. Kodaira.</i>

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.390
We're running out of time.

00:07:51.390 --> 00:07:53.700
We need to start catching students faster.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.060
Timothy, your voice.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.210
<i>Oh, I apolo—</i>

00:07:58.360 --> 00:07:59.510
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:03.050
Very good. I'm going back into the forest.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.290
Hunting like this makes me remember the past.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.140
I need to try harder to control myself.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.980
Burn, burn, burn...

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:17.360
Hibiki-chan and Ren-chan got caught.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.680
I wonder if Botan's still okay.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.930
I wouldn't even know where to start looking.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.660
Leave that to me, Hibari-chan!

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:26.770
I thought this might happen, so I 
learned a super special technique.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:28.580
Forehead Beam!

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.420
A super special technique?

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.230
Hand Power!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.500
Ready? I'm going to knock it over.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:34.450
Wait, are you...

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.430
Hanako, is that...

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.680
It's dowsing.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.450
That's not dowsing.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.340
What?!

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:51.700
I see.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.720
We're not looking for just one thing!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.820
Botan-chan and our carvings are 
in each of those directions!

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:58.890
R-Really?

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.360
If we follow each one, we'll find them all!

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:03.930
Let's do our best, Hibari-chan!

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:07.180
We only have one more hour...

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.730
But I guess we have no choice.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.850
Crack...

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.620
I found another one.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.760
Goodness...

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.890
Wh-What's going on?

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:44.730
Timo!

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.900
This game ends now!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:55.110
Looks like all these animals are female.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.860
That's it!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.590
Timo-mo!

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.880
Thanks.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.760
The great escape!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:18.340
Don't you think it's a little too hot?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.800
We'll just have to do it!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.060
Hibari has arrived!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.810
<b>Hibari
Hood</b>

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.810
Something like that.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.940
They say necessity knows no law...

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.960
Hibari Hood, can I have some water?

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.530
I told you, I'm not Hibari Hood.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.520
Hibari-chan, over there!

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:37.490
Is that your carving?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.950
We did it, Hibari-chan!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.400
Will you be okay? Be careful.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.210
Nothing to it!

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.420
Gotcha!

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:52.390
Huh?

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.090
That sound...

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.700
Hanako, get down here now!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:10:59.510
Okay.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.300
Hanako!

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:20.600
What was that?

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:25.700
<i>Girls, something seems to have 
happened by the flower garden.</i>

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.960
<i>I'm on my way to investigate,</i>

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.960
That's...

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.960
<i>so to be safe, don't go near it.</i>

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.590
What's wrong, Hibiki?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.710
Huh? Oh, right!

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.350
We need to avoid the flower garden, right?

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.930
Then let's go this way!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.360
But that way is...

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.590
Well, whatever.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.600
I need to hurry!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.270
Timo Punch!

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.410
<i>Timothy.</i>

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.150
Yeah, I heard you.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.340
An unexpected accident like this

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:06.960
must mean Hanakoizumi-san is involved.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:08.870
Could you go scout ahead of me?

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.830
Roger that. You guys handle things here.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:13.700
Timo!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.130
Totem pole.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.370
Is this...

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:33.060
Magma!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:35.710
Is this why it was so hot?

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:37.770
I can't believe it. This is insane!

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.540
Hanako, whatever you do, don't let go!

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:42.400
Okay.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.530
Hibari-san, Hanako-san!

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:51.600
Botan-chan!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.290
Botan?

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:56.360
Even if my arm breaks, I won't let go!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.460
I... I will save you!

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:00.920
Botan...

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.880
My leg is cramping...

00:13:10.710 --> 00:13:12.480
Ren-san, Hibiki-san...

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:14.520
What on earth is going on here?

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:18.400
I swear, only the craziest things
happen when I'm with you guys!

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:22.410
You can't say that after you
just charged into danger.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:23.610
Girls!

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.300
Timothy!

00:13:30.590 --> 00:13:31.200
Huh?

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:35.740
My moment to shine...

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:35.100
<b>Timo</b>

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.870
Timothy!

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.630
<i>An emergency whistle?</i>

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:47.380
Hanako!

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:49.050
Blow it!

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.030
<b>Tweet</b>

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.570
Teacher!

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.100
Timothy!

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.280
Got it!

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:18.300
Here we go!

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:27.760
We're saved...

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:30.720
That was a bit too adventurous.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.680
Teacher...

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:38.000
I caught you.

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:43.060
Our game of Miniature Garden Tag is now over.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:45.880
That might not be so bad...

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.780
The heart team has three members
and the star team has one.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:55.240
The four-leaf clover team is the 
only one with no survivors.

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.450
You're last place.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:15:01.170
<b>Camping Outside!!!</b>

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.240
We're camping outside!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.170
I can't believe it!

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:05.480
Hanako-san, you found your carving.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.570
Yeah!

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:07.210
Here.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.430
That's mine! Thank you!

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.920
I actually found these, too.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.860
That one's mine!

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.210
My futon.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.410
Wow! We found four of them.

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:24.730
No, five.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:26.190
That's mine.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.690
I-I just happened to find it, okay?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:33.130
They would've placed first 
if they hadn't gotten caught.

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:36.660
I'll have to come up with some
kind of reward for them.

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:38.840
Then say we don't have to sleep outside!

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:40.330
I can't do that.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.870
You can't?

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:44.640
B-But what about that huge hole?

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.630
Isn't it dangerous out here?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.420
We can't sleep outside!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:51.280
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.760
I know. That will be your reward.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.270
Heave-ho...

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.700
The water's nice.

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.190
That steam...

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.480
It wasn't magma. It was a hot spring.

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:10.690
Ren, don't fall asleep!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:14.160
We wouldn't stay somewhere that dangerous.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:16.000
What are you doing here?

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.840
Y-You're a boy! Peeping is
the definition of inappropriate!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.910
Robots aren't male or female.

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.660
It's okay for you to get in the water?

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.250
I'm waterproof.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.700
Timothy-san, thank you so 
much for putting together

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:33.220
such a wonderful hot spring.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.640
Unlike you, I'm just...

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:39.100
That's not true.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:43.180
You saved us earlier, and you 
even found two of the carvings.

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:46.000
Comparing yourself to others too much

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.250
is a classic negative trait.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:48.900
Huh?

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.530
That's what Ms. Kodaira said.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:51.530
Timo!

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.010
A negative trait, huh?

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.290
<i>Maybe I just don't realize it myself...</i>

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.620
Hey, what should we do?

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:06.040
About what?

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.840
About what we'll eat and where we'll sleep.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.740
Well...

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.550
Why don't you try thinking outside the box?

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.050
For example, we could build a 
tent with our picnic blankets.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:20.430
You can do that?

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.480
Of course.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:22.770
Amazing!

00:17:23.260 --> 00:17:25.730
There's plenty of food in the forest.

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:28.520
Oh! I'll go fishing!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.040
I'll help you, then.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.460
Let's do it together!

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.620
Sure. I wonder what we'll catch.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:39.450
Then I'll make something special 
with the ingredients you all gather.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.360
Really, Hibari-chan?

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.050
Hagyu-san, we'll help you pitch the tent, too.

00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:47.410
What's wrong?

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.690
I've been wondering for a while now,

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:51.880
but why do you only call me by my last name?

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:56.340
I thought you didn't want to be 
addressed by your first name.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.510
I don't.

00:17:57.960 --> 00:17:59.070
Then...

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.310
But I don't like it.

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:01.960
Huh?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.310
I don't like it when friends exclude me!

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:09.020
N-No! "Friends" was just a slip of the tongue!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.730
I don't think we're...

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.940
I get it, Hibiki.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.890
Your face is bright red.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:19.530
Shut up! I've just been in the hot water too long!

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:27.700
Found it!

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.940
Welcome back!

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:09.120
You're not sleeping?

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.320
It seems like a waste to sleep.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.530
You're right.

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:15.290
This outdoor school was rough, though.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.070
Huh? You think so?

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:21.520
Do you even realize what happened today?

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:22.280
Yeah.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.600
We played tag together, 
warmed up in the hot spring,

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:28.400
had a delicious meal,

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.620
and got to go camping, like we 
discussed before summer break.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:34.840
I had a super-duper fun time!

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.880
I'm really lucky!

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.380
Hanako, you're always so happy.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:44.920
Yeah!

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.030
<b>Fortune</b>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.030
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.030
<b>Great
Luck</b>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.030
<b>Anne-Happy</b>

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:09.030
<b>August 19
A Happy
Outdoor School</b>

00:23:02.580 --> 00:23:03.650
Good morning.

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:06.650
Good morning.

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.360
You seem to be in a good mood.

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:09.420
Huh?

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:16.670
Yeah, maybe a little.

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:32.540
Good morning, everyone.

00:23:38.530 --> 00:23:40.300
Good morning!

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:46.980
<b>All's happy that ends happy!</b>
